From e43e77c783a77734daf37a0250e95ee6b17f33b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 07:46:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04628/11362] [outer-loop] GAP-4891 Stage-2: relational
 goal-energy separates but does NOT guide search past the enumeration wall

Stage-2 lever (operator-directed) wires induce_goal_energy_relational into
graph_explore_solve_v2's goal_energy hook and tests energy-guided search vs a
BFS ablation, reproduction-gating both. On all 3 separating games
(cd82/sk48/sp80): induce_fired=True but NEITHER arm banks a new
reproduction-gated level -- both stall at L1 (4000 expansions, traj_len=0).

Decisive: separation is necessary but NOT sufficient -- ordering the frontier
by a correct goal-energy does not let the search REACH the next level because
the winning trajectory is never enumerated into the frontier. The within-game
deepening wall is trajectory ENUMERATION, the same wall as L1 first-contact --
converges independently with the conductor's .452 A1 WALL_DEEPER_THAN_VALUE_
PREDICTION. The relational energy is a genuine goal-DETECTION / verifier
contribution (survives the post-6/30 verifier-moat pivot) but is NOT the lever
that grows reproducible_total_levels.

adversarial_verify clean 3/3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
